<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: ICTU votes for talks on new national agreement.</title>
<headline>ICTU votes for talks on new national agreement.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Irish Congress of Trade Unions (ICTU) voted on Thursday to enter talks with the government and employers on a new national wage agreement.</p>
<p>But ICTU General Secretary Peter Cassells said the result did not mean that ICTU wanted a new agreement at any price. The next agreement must develop social partnership at the level of individual companies, Cassells said.</p>
<p>The current agreement between government, unions and employers, the Programme for Competitiveness and Work (PCW), expires at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 660 3377</p>
</text>
